57:**A fourth requirement belongs to this tool and not to the runner, and it is the one an implementer will miss: `--fail-on-scan-errors`.** TruffleHog treats a per-source scan error as non-fatal. Without that flag the process logs the error and **exits `0`**: a `filesystem` target that does not exist exits `0` with `encountered errors during scan` in the log (`07g`), and the same command with `--fail-on-scan-errors` exits `1` (`07h`). The sharper case is a partial scan — one readable target and one broken one — where the broken half is swallowed entirely and the exit reports only what the good half found: `183` without the flag, `1` with it (`07i`). A second route to the same silence is a `--since-commit` value the repository does not contain: the git source exits `0` having scanned `0` chunks (`07j`), which is an independent reason this decision recommends single-mode full history with no `--since-commit` at all. Kingfisher has no equivalent of either path, so this requirement is new with the ruling's tool rather than carried from revision 6.
