190-**Working directory, and the two rerun modes.** The script resolves every path it reads from its own location (`dirname "$0"`), so the working directory it is invoked from does not matter and no assertion consults git to *locate* a file; `13q` alone reads git history, and reads it to compare, not to find. **Mode 1, inside the repository:** `cd research/runs/R17/2026-09-05T163018Z-d7ade3a111f8/review/empirical`. **Mode 2, from a clean extraction with no repository at all:** `git archive --format=tar HEAD | tar -xf - -C <dir>`, then `cd <dir>/research/runs/R17/2026-09-05T163018Z-d7ade3a111f8/review/empirical`. Both modes run the same script over the same committed files; the only assertion that can tell them apart is `13q`, which compares the carried revision-2 copy with Git history and prints `SKIP` in mode 2 with that reason.
