194-**What varies across reruns, and the rule for comparing.** No log here is byte-for-byte reproducible and this decision does not claim one is. Rerunning a mode and diffing against its log gives at most **eight** printed regions that may differ, and I ran those diffs rather than predicting them. (1) Three timestamp lines: section 00's `UTC now:`, section 10's `counters below were read at:` and section 12's `read at:`. (2) The `mktemp` suffix inside the `$WORK` path, printed in section 00's `HOME used by this run:` line. (3) The live GitHub counters in section 10 (`stargazers_count`, `pushed_at`), which move whenever upstream does. (4) Section 00's `api.github.com core rate limit` line prints a `remaining` counter that moves with use — the `limit` beside it is asserted, the `remaining` is not. (5) The four absolute paths that name the extraction root — section 00's `decision under review:` and `carried revision 2:` and section 13's two — which differ with where the copy sits, and that is exactly how mode 2's log differs from mode 1's. (6) Section 00's gh and helper-toolchain resolution lines, which differ with the caller's `PATH`; the shim-path log is the deliberate demonstration. (7) Section 13's printed per-anchor digests, which move when an anchor already asserted to *differ* is edited. (8) The `SKIP` reason strings, which quote the probe values that produced them. **Two regions are upstream's rather than the host's and are called out separately:** section 09 prints `trufflesecurity/test_keys` at whatever HEAD it is cloned at — a **moving ref**, named as such in the log — and the verified count and detector names it yields are upstream's corpus, which is why `09a` asserts "at least one verified finding, exit 183" and not a fixed number. **The rerun-and-diff record, run rather than predicted.** Mode 1 was rerun after every anchor line section 13 reads was final, and diffed against the log cited above: **four differing lines** — the three timestamps and the `mktemp` suffix — and nothing else. All 62 `RESULT` verdicts matched, section 13's sixteen included. A reader who reruns it further apart in time will see a fifth: TruffleHog's star counter, which moved by one between two earlier runs in this revision and is printed for exactly that reason and never asserted. Mode 2 was rerun from a **second, independent `git archive HEAD` extraction** and diffed against its own log: **eight differing lines** — those same four, plus the four that print the extraction root. No `RESULT` line differed there either, its `13q` `SKIP` included. That second extraction is what makes the mode-2 claim a reproduction rather than a single lucky run. **How the mode-2 and mode-3 logs were produced, stated exactly rather than left to the commit graph.** The commit that carries this script did not exist while the script was being written, so those two logs were produced from an extraction of the parent commit with this revision's new files placed into it — a tree byte-identical to what the commit would archive. **That is a claim, so it was checked rather than asserted**: after commit `2de1598`, a genuine `git archive 2de1598` extraction was made and both archive modes were rerun inside it. Both exit `0`, and every `RESULT` label and verdict is identical to the committed logs' — `PASS=61 FAIL=0 SKIP=2` with declared inputs, `PASS=56 FAIL=0 SKIP=7` bare — compared label-by-label rather than by eye. The follow-up commit that records this sentence touches no line section 13 reads and no cited log. **The claim that survives any further editing, stated as the auditor can check it:** section 13 reads fourteen anchor lines and nothing else in this file. None of the **nine** asserted `same` has changed since before these logs were produced, and the **five** asserted to have moved are asserted on the verdict or on presence only, so editing one of them moves a printed digest and no `RESULT` line. Prose edited elsewhere in this document — this paragraph included — is not a line section 13 reads. One narrower claim, stated exactly: **no assertion in this script reads a moving branch ref.** The TruffleHog README and `main.go` are read at `v3.97.4`, the two source repositories at their programme pins, the gitleaks-action README at commit `bcfb9cce…` with its digest asserted (`11b`) — round 6's F2 is what taught this document that a README read from `master` is not evidence for a line number — and section 13's revision-2 source is pinned twice over, by digest in `13a` and against the commit in `13q`. The one moving ref anywhere in the run is the `test_keys` clone in section 09, which is printed and whose assertion is written not to depend on it. That is not the same as saying every asserted source is frozen: `10a`–`10d` assert on live GitHub metadata (a licence, an `archived` flag) and `11c` on a live licence field. Those are stable properties rather than counters, and if upstream changes one the assertion *should* fail — several are re-verify triggers. `00a`, `00b` and `00c` are the assertions that read the *host* rather than a remote source, and each is falsifiable there. The eight printed regions above are never asserted on. The comparison rule follows: a rerun of a given mode matches when every `RESULT <label>:` line matches in verdict, together with the closing `summary:` and `RESULT:` lines. The counter figures quoted in this document are read at these logs' retrieval instant and will drift.
